File streams: a slice of an open file ("fd:N:OFFSET:LENGTH")

Android stores the repack's groups uncompressed in the APK (androidResources' noCompress), and
AAsset_openFileDescriptor64 gives an asset as the APK's descriptor, the asset's offset and its length. StormLib opens
archives by name only, through its file provider, so the app copied each group out of the APK first (140 MB more on
the phone). The POSIX file provider now takes the name "fd:N:OFFSET:LENGTH": LENGTH bytes at OFFSET of the open file
N, read only. The stream reads them through a descriptor of its own (dup(N), closed with the stream; N stays its
owner's, who keeps it open while archives over it are) with pread at OFFSET plus the stream's offset, never past
LENGTH: the descriptors dup makes share one file position, and each thread opens an archive of its own over the same N.
A slice that does not lie within its file, or one opened to write, fails to open. Windows' provider is unchanged.

StormLib 9.40 has no stream of an application's own: its streams are a file, a mapped file, a file in an archive or a
URL, each opened by name (FileStream_OpenFile).

